  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##Exploration 3: Safer Social Media\r\n\r\n**Inquiry Question**: How can we update images that we provide to AI to account for safety and privacy?\r\n\r\n1. Choose one of the social media posts, drag it into the _Original Image_ section, and analyze possible data what you see. List data points visible within the post into three categories: public, private, and sensitive.\r\n2. Save your sketch into the backpack. Import the canvas into the AI Chat on Level 2 and ask it multiple questions about the person who might have made the social media post.\r\n3. Copy the image into the _Anonymized Image_ section. Drag and resize the black boxes to hide private or sensitive data in the image.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
